## C++ Structure
C++ is a compiled language. Every C++ program must have a `main()` function.

```cpp
#include <iostream>

int main() {
    std::cout << "Hello, World!" << std::endl;
    return 0;
}
```

## Java Structure
Everything in Java must be inside a class. The file name must match the class name.

```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Hello, World!");
    }
}
```

## Inheritance
Java uses the `extends` keyword for inheritance.

```java
class Animal {
    void eat() { System.out.println("Eating"); }
}
class Dog extends Animal {
    void bark() { System.out.println("Barking"); }
}
```
